    "nature_control_source_confounding": "High false positive AI rates (~60-70%) persist across all compression conditions on ImageNet nature images. This indicates that domain shift (ImageNet semantic distribution vs COCO training distribution) is a primary confounding factor alongside JPEG compression history.",
    "jpeg_compression_effect": "Re-compressing all images under JPEG Q95/Q75 does not eliminate domain confounding, confirming that synthetic format transformation does not erase historical sensor/compression provenance."
  },
  "caveats_and_limitations": [
    "This analysis is purely post-hoc and exploratory; results must not be used to choose winning models or claim generalization.",
